-- Free-text fields (bio, names, jsonb columns, etc.) are wrapped in
-- convert_from(decode('<base64>', 'base64'), 'UTF8') instead of plain quoted strings,
-- on purpose: it avoids any risk of a dropped escape on an apostrophe inside a long bio
-- corrupting the insert. Base64 has no characters that need escaping.
-- `region` keeps a plain quoted literal - it's a real enum (application_region) and
-- needs to stay an unknown-typed literal for Postgres's implicit cast to work.

